Hail, fellow nethackers!

Having recently downloaded the entire extremely massive NetHack 3.0
patchlevel 9 source, I was naturally interested in getting it to run
on my 80286-based machine running DOS 3.3.  I do not, however, have
Microsoft C 5.1, as recommended for the use of the overlay manager.  I
DO, however, have Borland Turbo C++ 1.0, which includes the so-called
"VROOMM" (virtual runtime object-oriented memory management) overlay
system.  Examination of the documentation for the overlay
manager included with NetHack 3.0 revealed that it uses a strategy not
entirely unlike Borland's.  However, I have been unsuccessful so far
in getting the code to function with Borland's overlay system.

My gut feeling is:  "Darn it, if it worked for Quattro Pro, it
_oughta_ work for NetHack!" :-)

My question is:  Has anyone else played around with Turbo C++, VROOMM,
and NetHack 3.0, and managed to get something to work?  If so, would
you be willing to share a few tips and/or instructions?

Please reply by e-mail unless you think it's of general enough
interest to post.
